# Copy to .env and fill in. agent.py loads .env from this directory at startup.
# A real .env holds a live secret: keep it out of version control.
#
# Which key you need depends on the speech mode:
#   --speech cloud (what start_booth.sh runs by default):      GOOGLE_API_KEY
#   --speech local (agent.py default; Whisper + Claude + TTS):  ANTHROPIC_API_KEY
#
# GOOGLE_API_KEY (GEMINI_API_KEY also works) comes from Google AI Studio:
#   https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
# Gemini's Google Search grounding needs billing enabled on that project;
# without it the agent logs "web search: unavailable" and runs without it.

GOOGLE_API_KEY=

# This must be an Anthropic API key, from:
#   https://console.anthropic.com/settings/keys
#
# A Claude Code / Claude.ai subscription will NOT work here. That credential
# authenticates Claude Code itself; API traffic from your own applications is a
# separate product with separate billing. There is no way to point this agent at
# a subscription.
#
# If you would rather not keep a key on disk at all, skip this file entirely:
#   ant auth login
#   .venv/bin/python agent.py --auth oauth

ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...
